=== Step 2: your choices ===
  [ok] model: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (Unsloth)

  1) UD-IQ4_XS ~4-bit i-quant (Unsloth Dynamic), between IQ3_S and UD-Q4_K_XL in quality; on a PC with less than ~80 GB of RAM part of its experts are read from the SSD; download 94 GB, keeps ~55 GB of its 60 GB of experts in RAM
  2) UD-Q4_K_XL 4-bit (Unsloth Dynamic), EXPERIMENTAL: the best quality, but most experts come from the SSD on a 64 GB PC (7-8.5 tokens/s measured); download 111 GB, keeps ~71 GB of its 77 GB of experts in RAM
  [ok] UD-IQ4_XS on GPU 0 (Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB, 16 GB) + GPU 1 (Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB, 16 GB) + GPU 2 (Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB, 16 GB) + GPU 3 (Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB, 16 GB), as you chose (--gpus): no RAM budget - all of its experts (~60 GB) are loaded into RAM from the model files at start, and the files pass through the OS file cache (needs ~118 GB of RAM, this PC has 122)
  [ok] size: UD-IQ4_XS

  Context length = how much text the model can see at once (your chat, files, tool output).
  Longer needs more VRAM for it, so fewer experts fit on the GPU:
  1) 8K tokens
  2) 32K tokens   (recommended for your GPU)
  3) 64K tokens
  4) 128K tokens
  5) 256K tokens
  6) 384K tokens   (experimental: setup adds rope scaling)
  7) 512K tokens   (experimental: setup adds rope scaling)
  [ok] context: 32768 tokens
  [ok] KV cache: 8-bit
  [ok] images: off

